flowchart LR
  accTitle: Five distinct objects often called shared context
  accDescr: A message is a transport unit. A shared store or blackboard is an addressable representation. An agent team determines who participates. A communication topology defines which agents can exchange messages. A content coalition bundles typed evidence or proposals for bounded workspace admission. B3 concerns the final object rather than the other four.
  M[Message] --> MT[Transport]
  S[Shared store or blackboard] --> ST[Addressable state]
  A[Agent team] --> AT[Who participates]
  G[Communication topology] --> GT[Who can communicate]
  C[Typed content coalition] --> CT[What enters bounded workspace]
  CT --> B[B3 candidate object]
